# ---- Old Jack's conversation ----
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.first_words.text = Don't mind the head. It's a pumpkin, and it's been on there a long while.\nI'm Old Jack. Every autumn the dead get restless, so I come back to the <color is="#ffd97a">Forgotten Temple</color> with my lanterns. I could use a pair of hands that aren't carved.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.first_words.opt.hail = Pleased to meet you, Jack.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.meet.text = You found the place, then. Don't mind the head, it's a pumpkin.\nI'm Old Jack. The dead get restless this time of year, and my lanterns keep them off these steps. Everybody who finds me gets a <b>welcome</b>, and you haven't had yours yet.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.meet.opt.accept = Thanks, Jack.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.board_fresh.text = There's fresh work on my board, some for the dark and some for the daylight. Ask me what needs doing. It pays in sweets, and my shop takes those.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.menu.text = The lanterns are lit and the ghouls are out walking. What do you need?
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.patch_offer.text = See the lanterns on these steps? Every one of them started as a pumpkin that came up cold to the touch, glowing a little. <b>Hallowed Pumpkins</b>, I call those.\nBring me a few and I'll carve some more.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.patch_offer.opt.accept = I'll find you some pumpkins.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.patch_ready.text = <b>Hallowed Pumpkins</b>. Cold as a cellar step.\nI've put a few Lantern Bombs in with your pay. Go and see how they burn.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.patch_ready.opt.turnin = Here are the pumpkins.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.lantern_work_offer.text = A <b>Lantern Bomb</b> is a pumpkin packed with powder and a short fuse. Light it and throw it. Then stand back.\nThrow a few at something that has it coming, and come and tell me how they went.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.lantern_work_offer.opt.accept = I'll throw a few.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ghouls_offer.text = <b>Hollow Ghouls</b> crawl out of the old graves after dark, and they come out hungry.\nPut a few of them back in the ground before they find the temple steps.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ghouls_offer.opt.accept = I'll deal with the ghouls.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.souls_offer.text = Poor things, the <b>Lost Souls</b>. They drift about until somebody lets them go.\nSet a few free and bring me the <b>Ectoplasm</b> they leave behind. My lanterns drink the stuff.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.souls_offer.opt.accept = I'll set them free.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.geodes_offer.text = A <b>Cursed Geode</b> is a lump of stone with something bright moving inside. Ugly things.\nCrack a few open. There's good in them, under the curse.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.geodes_offer.opt.accept = I'll crack some open.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.rider_offer.text = You've heard the hooves at night? That's the <b>Headless Horseman</b>, riding his graveyard.\nI'd sleep better if somebody knocked him off that horse. The <color is="#ffd97a">Gravekeeper</color> beside me won't open the gate till he's burned a <b>Grave Candle</b> at it, and I sell those at my shop once I count you a Regular. Buy one, then go and get him.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.rider_offer.opt.accept = I'll knock him off it.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ember_offer.text = You've seen my errands through, and you've had the Horseman off his horse. That's near enough everything.\nYour <b>Hollow Lantern</b> wants a flame that won't go out, and only the Horseman carries one. Take it off him and bring me <b>the Horseman's Ember</b>. He only carries it on the hard ride, and the Gravekeeper won't open that gate without a <b>Burning Grave Candle</b>. I sell those once you're Trusted with me.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ember_offer.opt.accept = I'll bring you the ember.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.active_ember.text = He only gives that ember up on the hard ride. Ask the <color is="#ffd97a">Gravekeeper</color> for the <b>hard ride</b>, and bring more friends than last time. His gate wants a <b>Burning Grave Candle</b> for it, and I sell those once you're Trusted with me.\nOnce he's down, the <b>ember</b> waits in the chest where he fell, for whoever I sent after it. Miss the chest and it waits under Claims in your menu.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ember_ready.text = That's his fire, all right. Burned through your pocket, by the look of it.\nI'll keep it safe till your lantern's ready. Then we light it.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ember_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the ember.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.daily_offer.text = I've got a few small jobs that come round every day. Take what you like.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.daily_offer.opt.souls = I'll see to the souls.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.daily_offer.opt.pumpkins = I'll bring pumpkins.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.daily_offer.opt.geodes = I'll crack some geodes.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.lantern_offer.text = Your errands are done, and I've got the Horseman's ember. So this year we light a <b>Hollow Lantern</b> for you.\nSome of the skeletons out there wear my face, and I don't care for it. Knock a few <b>Jack Skeletons</b> down, then bring me a <b>Hallowed Pumpkin</b> to carve and some <b>Ectoplasm</b> to burn in it.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.lantern_offer.opt.accept = Let's light it.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.lantern_ready.text = A <b>Hallowed Pumpkin</b>, and <b>Ectoplasm</b> to burn in it. The skeletons with my face are down in the grass where they belong.\nThere. The ember took. Your Hollow Lantern's lit, and it's yours to keep. Take this shield as well: my shop sells the helm, and the Horseman wears the rest of the set. Come back next year and we'll light another.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.lantern_ready.opt.turnin = Here's the pumpkin, and the Ectoplasm.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.active_pumpkins.text = Pumpkins grow wild in the <color is="#ffd97a">autumn woods</color>, and the <color is="#ffd97a">Kweebecs</color> keep them in their gardens. Pick them by hand and every so often there's a <b>Hallowed Pumpkin</b> among them. The <b>Jack Skeletons</b> drop them too, after dark.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.active_bombs.text = Throw the <b>Lantern Bombs</b> from your pay at whatever comes for you after dark. Run short and my shop has more, and the <b>Jack Skeletons</b> drop a few.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.active_night.text = The dead walk after dark, out in the wild and away from any torch. Gone by dawn.\nA <b>Lost Soul</b> leaves <b>Ectoplasm</b> when you set it free, and a <b>Jack Skeleton</b> sometimes drops a <b>Hallowed Pumpkin</b>.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.active_stone.text = Break <b>stone</b>, <b>ore</b> most of all, and now and then a <b>Cursed Geode</b> falls out. Hold one in your hand and crack it open.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ready_generic.text = That looks done to me. Let's see it.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.ready_generic.opt.turnin = It's done.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.lantern_lit.text = That's this year's Hollow Lantern lit. Set it out somewhere the dead can see it.\nWhat do you need?
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.sweets.text = My shop takes them for everything on it, from a Lantern Bomb to a head like mine.\nI pay them for my jobs and the work on my board. Ask anybody you talk to for a trick or treat and you'll get a few. Beat the <b>Headless Horseman</b> in his <color is="#ffd97a">graveyard</color> and you'll find some waiting for you too.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.who_are_you.text = Old Jack. I kept a farm once, a long way from here. Then one October I didn't go home, and I've come back every October since.\nMy lanterns keep the dead off these steps, and every year I light a Hollow Lantern with anybody who sees my errands through. Don't ask me about the head.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.horseman.text = The <b>Headless Horseman</b>. He rides his own graveyard every night of Hallow's Eve. He's half fire himself, so my Lantern Bombs only do him half the harm, but they still bite.\nThe <color is="#ffd97a">Gravekeeper</color> next to me keeps the gate. He'll take you in once he's burned a <b>Grave Candle</b> at it, and I sell those at my shop once I count you a Regular. Whoever goes in first pays, and the rest of the party follows free. Bring friends, and when his head flies off, cut it down, or he can't be hurt.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.horseman_beaten.text = So you knocked him off that horse. It won't keep him down: he's back in the saddle every time somebody goes in.\nGo after the <b>Headless Horseman</b> again if you like. Your first win each day leaves two Claims in the chest where he falls: his daily Claim, and his Boss Kill Claim, which now and then holds a piece of his old armour, or one that's still burning. Whatever you leave in it waits under Claims in your menu.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.harvest_moon.text = See that moon? Harvest Moon. A few nights a year the dead get restless under it, and the graves empty out.\nIf you want work, tonight's the night. I'll be up till it sets.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.quests = What needs doing?
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.shop = Let's see your shop.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.sweets = What are the sweets for?
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.standing = How do we stand?
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.almanac = Show me the Almanac.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.horseman = Tell me about the Horseman.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.who = Who are you?
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.harvest = What's a Harvest Moon?
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.back = Something else.
dialogue.hallows_eve_old_jack.opt.farewell = Goodnight, Jack.

# ---- Trick-or-treat, the line every conversation gets ----
dialogue.hallows_eve_trick_or_treat.opt.knock = Trick or treat.

# ---- The Gravekeeper's conversation (he never contracts) ----
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.menu.text = The Horseman's <color is="#ffd97a">graveyard</color> is behind me, and he is riding it tonight. Nothing in there rests while he does.\nThe gate opens only when I burn a <b>Grave Candle</b> at it, and once it is open, your whole party may follow you in. Old Jack sells them at his shop, once he counts you a Regular. An <b>Eternal Candle</b> opens it as well, and that one I give back. Say the word and I will take you in. Bring friends.
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.who.text = I keep this graveyard so the dead in it can rest. I am one of the <b>Hallowed</b>, and we put down whatever will not.\nThe dead stir under a full moon, and on Hallow's Eve they hardly sleep at all. The <b>Headless Horseman</b> never rests, so somebody has to keep knocking him down.
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.hard_open.text = You knocked him off his horse. He has not forgotten it.\nThere is a <b>hard ride</b> now, for anyone who comes back. He hits harder on it, and what he drops there, he drops nowhere else. For that gate I burn a <b>Burning Grave Candle</b>, and Old Jack sells those once you're Trusted with him.
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.ember.text = Jack sent you for <b>the Horseman's Ember</b>. He only carries it on the <b>hard ride</b>, and for that gate I burn a <b>Burning Grave Candle</b>. Jack sells those once you're Trusted with him.\nOnce he is down, it waits in the chest where he fell for every one of you Jack sent after it. Nobody else will find it. Miss the chest and it waits under Claims in your menu.
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.opt.enter = Take me in. (1 Grave Candle)
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.opt.enter_hard = Take me on the hard ride. (1 Burning Grave Candle)
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.opt.who = Who are you?
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.opt.back = Something else.
dialogue.hallows_eve_gravekeeper.opt.farewell = Goodnight.

