# ---- The Almanac page's items: where each comes from ----
almanac.hallows_eve.source.pumpkin = Found now and then when you pick pumpkins by hand, and dropped by Jack Skeletons and Pumpkin Fiends.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.geode = Found in the rock and ore you mine, and dropped by Geode Wraiths.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.ectoplasm = Dropped by Lost Souls, and found inside Cursed Geodes.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.bombs = Dropped by the night's creatures, found inside Cursed Geodes, carved at a Carving Bench, or bought at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.bomb_epic = Rarely dropped by Geode Wraiths or found inside Cursed Geodes and the Hallowed's cache. You can also carve one at a Carving Bench, or buy a couple a day at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.trick_or_treat = Handed out when you go trick-or-treating.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.workbench = Built at a Workbench, any time of year.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.carved = Carved at a Carving Bench, or bought at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.jack_shield = Carved at a Carving Bench, or bought at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.burning_helm = Sold at Old Jack's shop once the Hallowed revere you or Old Jack trusts you completely.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.flaming_shield = Sold at Old Jack's shop once the Hallowed hold you in the highest regard.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.stall = Sold at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.grave_candle = Sold at Old Jack's shop once he counts you a Regular, and given back by the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim: sometimes one after your first win each day, and a few after your first hard win. The Gravekeeper burns them to open his graveyard for your party, and once you're Trusted with Old Jack he trades a Burning Grave Candle for a handful.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.burning_grave_candle = Sold at Old Jack's shop once you're Trusted with him, or traded there for a handful of Grave Candles. The Gravekeeper burns them to open the Headless Horseman's hard ride for your party.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.stall_or_lab = Sold at Old Jack's shop as your standing grows, or built at the Goblin Tinkerer's Workbench in the goblin lab.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.festival_stall = Sold on the festival shelf at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.keepsake = Old Jack's keepsake, given once a year when you finish his story.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.festival_favor = Sold at the festival shops to those high in Festival Favor.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.bomb_rare = Always in the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim, and sometimes in his daily Claim. Also dropped by the night's creatures, found inside Cursed Geodes, carved at a Carving Bench, or bought at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.bomb_epic_horseman = Rarely dropped by Geode Wraiths or found inside Cursed Geodes and the Hallowed's cache, and sometimes in the Headless Horseman's daily Claim. You can also carve one at a Carving Bench, or buy a couple a day at Old Jack's shop.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.hoard = Sometimes in the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim, paid for your first win over him each day.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.hoard_hard = Only in the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim on the hard ride, paid for your first hard win over him each day. Once you've finished The Rider, ask the Gravekeeper for the hard ride.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.hoard_normal = Only in the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim on the normal ride, paid for your first win over him there each day.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.eternal_candle = Now and then in the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim on the hard ride, paid for your first hard win over him each day. Carry it and the Gravekeeper opens his normal graveyard for your party without burning a Grave Candle.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.burning_helm_trade = Bought at Old Jack's shop by trading in a Jack Helm from your bag, once the Hallowed revere you or Old Jack trusts you completely. Sometimes found in the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim.
almanac.hallows_eve.source.flaming_shield_trade = Bought at Old Jack's shop by trading in a Jack Shield from your bag, once the Hallowed hold you in the highest regard. Sometimes found in the Horseman's Boss Kill Claim.

# ---- The Almanac page's Headless Horseman banner and his Boss Kill Claim ----
almanac.hallows_eve.horseman.line = The Gravekeeper next to Old Jack takes you in. Bring friends.
almanac.hallows_eve.horseman.button = Boss fight records
almanac.hallows_eve.hoard.line = Your first win each day leaves his Boss Kill Claim in the chest where he falls, and under Claims: a Spectral Lantern Bomb and favor with Old Jack, and sometimes a Grave Candle, a piece of his armour, a piece of the Flaming Hallowed set, a Tombstone or a Lost Civilization Lantern. On the hard ride it holds a few Grave Candles and the Hallowed's favor, better odds at his armour and the flaming pieces, his flaming breastplate and, once in a while, an Eternal Candle.

